course: dictionary
lesson: 5896
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word maple can name a tree, the hard wood of that tree, or a sweet syrup. «Some seeds are carried by the wind, like dandelion and maple seeds» is about the tree, because seeds come from plants, not wood.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. «Canada's red maple leaf flag was adopted in 1965» uses maple to describe a leaf, so maple here is part of a phrase: a maple leaf is a leaf from a maple tree. When a word looks new, try the words around it before you reach for a dictionary.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If you think maple means a tree and the sentence says «the maple's leaf is shaped like an open hand», does it still make sense? Yes, so the tree meaning fits. Always test your guess this way.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have several meanings; the context shows which one is right.
fact: A maple is a tree whose leaves have pointed parts like fingers.
fact: In autumn, maple leaves turn red, orange or yellow.
fact: «Maple» can also mean the hard wood of the tree, or the sweet syrup made from the sap of some maple trees.
fact: «Canada's red maple leaf flag» was adopted in 1965, so the maple leaf is a symbol of Canada.
fact: Maple seeds have wings and spin like helicopters as they fall.
exercise: «Some seeds are carried by the wind, like dandelion and maple seeds.» What kind of thing is a maple in this sentence? | A sweet syrup | A type of bird | A tree that makes seeds | *A tree
exercise: «The maple's leaf is shaped like an open hand.» Which part of a maple tree has pointed parts like fingers? | The roots | The seeds | The bark | *The leaves
exercise: «Sycamore is a kind of maple, and maple seeds grow in winged pairs.» Which of these is a kind of maple? | Oak | Dandelion | Horse chestnut | *Sycamore
test: «Sycamore seeds have a wing that makes them spin as they fall, slowing them down.» What makes sycamore seeds spin as they fall? | Their roots | Their weight alone | *A wing | Strong wind only
test: Maple can mean a tree, its wood, or its syrup. Which meaning is the hard wood of this tree? | A sweet syrup poured on pancakes | *The hard wood of the maple tree | The tree itself | A kind of bird
exam: What is the symbol on the flag of Canada? | A sunflower | A lion | *A red maple leaf | A bear
